        "file": "test-cases/eslint-snippets/fixture/executor-library-terminal/controls.ts",
        "line": 30,
        "message": "This callback only forwards to read. Call that executor on the SQL text (`read(sql)`, or `const exec = read; exec(sql)`). Passing the function into a helper (`write(sql`SELECT id FROM widgets WHERE id = ${id}`, {\n    ...options,\n    query: read,\n  })`) does not connect the statement to the executor, so analysis cannot see it.",
        "messageId": "forward",
        "ruleId": "no-mistakes/postgres-no-executor-adapter",
        "severity": 2
      },
      {
        "column": 82,
        "endColumn": 87,
        "endLine": 35,
        "file": "test-cases/eslint-snippets/fixture/executor-library-terminal/controls.ts",
        "line": 35,
        "message": "This call passes other into a helper. Name the executor inside the helper (`other(sql`…`)`) instead of passing it. Analysis does not follow an executor passed as a value, so this call is not a judged rewrite. Write the SQL as an argument of that executor. Analysis cannot check SQL that only reaches the executor through a passed function.",
        "messageId": "passed",
        "ruleId": "no-mistakes/postgres-no-executor-adapter",
        "severity": 2
      },
      {
        "column": 27,
        "endColumn": 4,
        "endLine": 62,
        "file": "test-cases/eslint-snippets/fixture/executor-library-terminal/controls.ts",
        "line": 59,
        "message": "This adapter hides write from SQL analysis (arity or rest). Call the executor on the SQL text (`write(sql)`, or `const exec = write; exec(sql)`). `selectWidget(id, write)` is not a judged rewrite: analysis does not follow an executor passed as a value. Write the direct call explicitly. Analysis cannot check SQL that only reaches the executor through this adapter.",
        "messageId": "blocked",
        "ruleId": "no-mistakes/postgres-no-executor-adapter",
        "severity": 2
      },
